  "summary": "Kathputli is a string puppet theatre native to Rajasthan, India, and is the most popular form of Indian puppetry.",
  "description": "Kathputli is a string puppet theatre native to Rajasthan, India, and is the most popular form of Indian puppetry. Being a string marionette, it is controlled by a single string that passes it from the top of the puppet over the puppeteers.\n\nPutli meaning a doll. Kathputli means a puppet which is made entirely from wood. However it is made out of wood, cotton cloth and metal wire.",
  "culturalContext": "Registered as a Geographical Indication of India (handicraft, Rajasthan; registration 2008–09), which protects the name for products made in its place of origin by traditional methods.",
